# ---- blind PR lists (BH-847, optional) ----
# Every lane that lists PRs bumps a per-(lane, repo) counter in
# state/blind-list/ when the list fails for a TRANSIENT reason (an invisible repo
# and an exhausted API bucket keep their own single alert and are not counted).
# At this many CONSECUTIVE failures, one ALERTS.log line and one fleet_alert beat
# say how long that lane has been blind on that repo and what it blocks; further
# ticks stay quiet until a list works. Both knobs read the `blind_ticks_alert` /
# `blind_ticks_window_secs` settings rows FIRST (bin/jobs-client.sh setting-set),
# so these lines are the documented fallback, not the source of truth. Code
# fallback is 3, and a value that is not a tick count logs a line and uses 3.
#BLIND_TICKS_ALERT=3
# How far apart two failures can be and still count as consecutive. A lane that
# never reports a success cannot accumulate a streak across unrelated days, and a
# new streak also clears the dedupe flag so the next real outage still pages.
#BLIND_TICKS_WINDOW_SECS=7200

